     frequency: the entry's capacitors take the pulse and TRK_VS peaks at 25.16 V, under D4's least breakdown at the cold
     end, 29.70 V)
     D2: D4 at 5 A 36.06 V (25 C) and 37.34 V (hot end); the bound U5 0.1350 V and U18 0.1277 V; the loaded network U5
     0.0766 V, TRK_VS 25.02 V, PV_P 25.08 V, D4 0.00 A; the pulse's charge 0.160 uC, the trip filter's excursion at most
     0.000081 A; D4's energy with the whole pulse in it 0.0060 mJ. The loop current the test may drive is not limited by
     the standard: U5's rating is reached at 15.7 A with the whole current through R59 (the bound) and at 64 A in the
     loaded network; D4's clamp reaches the drafted entry's 50 V at 43.1 A
     D4 with the drafted SMCJ28A: a stiff 36 V through the lead into the clamp (INFERRED straight line from each breakdown
     at the printed slope); D4's continuous capability on the board, from TJ 150 C and RthJA 75 C/W (typical, 8 x 8 mm
     pads), is 1.17 W at the hot end's air and 2.27 W at the cold end's (the sheet's 6.5 W is on an infinite heat sink):
       the least part at the cold end               breakdown 29.70 V:  16.63 A,   585.8 W
       the least part at 25 C                       breakdown 31.10 V:  12.94 A,   457.9 W
       the highest part at 25 C                     breakdown 34.40 V:   4.22 A,   151.2 W
       the least part at the junction's maximum     breakdown 34.99 V:   2.67 A,    95.9 W
     so D4 conducts amps at any junction temperature it can reach and is over its rating by two orders of magnitude; the
     sheet's typical failure mode is a short, which F2 then clears; every other part of the drafted entry is rated above 36
     V (the bulk and C71 to C74 50 V, U18 75 V, U5 80 V, Q3 60 V); as drawn, C11 and C12 are 35 V, under it. The largest
     sustained source the drafted entry holds is D4's least breakdown at the cold end, 29.70 V (under it D4 carries less
     than its 1 mA test current)
     THE TVS-ONLY CHANGE for D4, evaluated and not taken (superseded by THE SOLAR-FAULT REMEDIES below), read from the held
     series (Littelfuse SMCJ p.2): the least row that stands off 36 V and does not break down at the cold end is SMCJ36A
     (VR 36.0 V, VBR 40.00 to 44.20 V, 38.20 V at the cold end; VC 58.1 V at 25.9 A). Alone it does not hold the derived
     set on the drafted entry: under REQ-016's criterion D1's 10 A plateau puts its clamp at 49.57 V at 25 C and 51.21 V at
     the hot end (typical coefficient), against the 50 V parts; the 50 V parts are reached at 10.81 A (25 C) and 7.75 A
     (hot end), Q3's 60 V at 29.4 A. So the change that holds every derived disturbance is SMCJ36A WITH the entry's 50 V
     parts at the 63 V class: the bulk C11, C12 and C69 to EEHZA1J220XP (22 uF 63 V in the same 6.3 x 7.7 mm D8 land, ESR
     80 mOhm against 40, ZA p.2), which takes the bulk ahead of the bank from 99 uF to 66 uF and so re-opens the CS101
     correction (re-run with it), and C71 to C74 at 63 V or more (no ceramic's sheet is held); and with it a 36 V source
     runs the stage, whose input is then the regulation's 105.73 W to the trip's 135.26 W at 36 V, outside REQ-016's window
     (a single fault for layer 8). The alternative that also closes D5 is an input over-voltage and reverse disconnect
     ahead of PV_P (a series FET with its controller): more parts, and no sheet for one is held
     D5: D4's forward path carries 6.802 A held; on the board it can dissipate 1.17 W at the hot end, so it holds only
     below a forward drop of 0.172 V, which no silicon junction has at that current (INFERRED; the sheet prints the forward
     drop at 100 A only): NOT MET as DECISION-31 recorded (E-N1, board E's owner); the keyed receptacle is the barrier
     against it
